    "result": "Excellent! All tests are now passing. Here's a summary of the fixes I made:\n\n## Issue 1: Toxicity Metric Score Incorrect\n**Problem**: The `toxicityMetric` function was receiving `references` as its second parameter but treating them as `bannedTerms`. This caused false positives when scanning outputs for toxic content.\n\n**Fix**: Updated the function signature from `toxicityMetric(outputs, bannedTerms)` to `toxicityMetric(outputs, references, bannedTerms)` so that when `runEvaluations` calls it with both outputs and references, the parameters align correctly.\n\n## Issue 2: APPROVAL_STATUSES Undefined\n**Problem**: The test file imports `APPROVAL_STATUSES` as a named export from `./index.js`, but it was only available through the default export, not as a direct named export.\n\n**Fix**: Added explicit re-exports in `packages/frai-core/src/finetune/index.js` for `APPROVAL_STATUSES`, `DATA_SENSITIVITY_LEVELS`, `GOVERNANCE_SECTIONS`, and `RISK_LEVELS` so they can be imported directly.\n\n## Test Results\n\u2705 **All 28 tests passing** (8 test files):\n- `src/eval/index.test.js` \u2713 (3 tests)\n- `src/finetune/governance.test.js` \u2713 (5 tests)\n- Plus 6 other test files with 20 additional tests",
